<title>USA: Judge recommends Loewen injunction.</title>
<headline>Judge recommends Loewen injunction.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Service Corp International said Monday that U.S. Magistrate Judge Nancy Johnson has issued a memorandum recommending that District Judge John Rainey of the U.S. District Court for the Southern District of Texas issue a temporary restraining order prohibiting The Loewen Group Inc from proceeding with its antitrust suit against Service Corp in federal court in New York.</p>
<p>Service Crop said that Judge Johnson also recommended that Judge Rainey issue an injunction against Loewen proceeding with its Brooklyn suit until further order of the Court.  </p>
<p>Service Corp said that Judge Johnson's action was a recommendation only and would not be binding on Loewen unless ordered by the District Court Judge.</p>
</text>
